research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl-32-{"id":"thm-complete-and-totally-bounded-uniform-spaces-are-compact","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Complete-plus-precompact implies compact is standard, but the item explicitly assumes only the ultrafilter lemma, whereas the source works classically. The local proof verifies that weaker assumption; its extra full-Choice citation is an A3 defect. ALPHA CONCURRENCE: Complete plus totally bounded implies compact is a classical uniform-space theorem. The proof through convergence of ultrafilters uses precisely the ultrafilter lemma; making that weak-choice hypothesis explicit is a standard foundational calibration, not invention.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl-33-{"id":"cor-uniform-compactness-equivalence","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://encyclopediaofmath.org/wiki/Uniform_space"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Compact iff complete and totally bounded is standard, but the item records the precise ultrafilter-lemma assumption for the reverse implication. No located source states that same foundational calibration. ALPHA CONCURRENCE: The compactness equivalence is the classical combination of compact-implies-complete, compact-implies-totally-bounded, and the converse. Its explicit ultrafilter-lemma scope is a faithful foundational restatement of established mathematics.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl-34-{"id":"lem-finite-star-refinement-for-compact-hausdorff-spaces","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"The compact-Hausdorff uniformization proofs in the sources construct finite open refinements with the required star control. The item extracts that standard construction as a named lemma.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl-35-{"id":"thm-compact-hausdorff-open-cover-uniformity","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources construct the unique compatible uniformity on a compact Hausdorff space from diagonal neighborhoods and open covers. The item uses the equivalent cover formulation. Its final entourage recovery fails for the locally admitted empty compact space.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl-36-{"id":"thm-compact-hausdorff-space-has-a-unique-compatible-uniformity","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"Vienna Theorem 9.4.14 and Wodzicki Corollary 4.8 give uniqueness, with Vienna also giving existence, under the standard nonempty convention. The library admits empty compact Hausdorff space but no uniformity on it, so the exactly-one claim needs nonemptiness.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl:37:{"id":"cor-compact-domain-maps-are-uniformly-continuous","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf"],"rationale":"Wodzicki Theorem 4.7 and BIU state the compact-domain theorem for the natural compatible uniformity. The library convention requires a nonempty domain, and the proof needs the cover dictionary cited explicitly.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl-38-{"id":"def-countably-based-uniformity","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources define a uniform base by cofinal refinement and countable base exactly as the item does.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl-39-{"id":"lem-countable-uniform-base-normalisation","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Decreasing symmetric bases with triple-composite control are the standard metrization normalization, but the item emphasizes its finite-intersection recursion works in ZF. No located source states this exact choice-free proposition. ALPHA CONCURRENCE: Normalizing a countable entourage base to a decreasing symmetric base with triple-composite control is the standard first step in uniform-space metrization. Choosing least indices in a fixed enumeration makes the usual construction choice-free, so the ZF form remains established mathematics.","alpha_concurred":true,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl-40-{"id":"thm-countably-based-uniformity-is-pseudometrizable","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf","https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources give pseudometrizability of countably based uniformities and the separated criterion for the pseudometric to distinguish points. The item packages both; its metric criterion needs a direct metric-definition citation.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl-41-{"id":"def-uniformizable-space","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"Wodzicki and Vienna define uniformizable as having a compatible uniformity; the item additionally names the standard separated variant without altering either definition.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-topology-uniform.provenance.jsonl-42-{"id":"lem-uniformizable-spaces-are-regular","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources state the regularity consequence of a compatible uniformity with the same non-T1 convention. The proof is the standard entourage-shrinking argument.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
